{% doc %}
  Theme Drawer Infrastructure

  Loads the theme-drawer Web Component. Rendered once from layout/theme.liquid.

  Individual drawer snippets (e.g. chat-drawer) render their own
  <theme-drawer> elements. Shared structural CSS is inlined here.

  Horizon also coordinated three things from this file: it squeezed
  .page-wrapper aside while a drawer was open on wide viewports, saved the
  open drawer ids to sessionStorage, and reopened them synchronously during
  parsing on the next page so the squeezed layout rendered on first paint.

  All three came out with the move to an overlay drawer (see MODAL_QUERY in
  assets/theme-drawer.js). Nothing squeezes now, so there is no layout to
  restore -- and the restore path set the [open] attribute directly rather
  than calling showModal(), which for a modal dialog would put it on the page
  without its backdrop, its scroll lock or the top layer. Horizon's own
  comment made the same argument for phones, where the drawer was already an
  overlay: let it start closed after navigation rather than reopen a
  fullscreen dialog the reader has moved on from.

  @example
  {% render 'theme-drawer' %}
{% enddoc %}

{% render 'theme-drawer-styles' %}

<script
  type="module"
  src="{{ 'theme-drawer.js' | asset_url }}"
  fetchpriority="low"
></script>
